Well, please don't take this in the wrong way.  It's meant
to be (semi) humorous.
But I've found a way to reduce the benifits of polypiling.
You simply say to the person polypiling:
YOU WIMP!  I can get down and back from hell in about 12
hours!  Never mind that in my haste last game I polymorphed
the wizard and accidentally polymorph the amulet (damn).
But get real.  You're not going to impress anyone with the
stuff you get from polypiling.  All I need is an excaliber,
3 wishes in case I didn't find vitally needed things, and
that's it.  The last game I won I only had an athame.  With
speed boots & teleport control, you really don't need much.
If you think you need an AC better than -15 to win, you must 
not be a that sharp.  No wonder you're bored.

p.s. In all honesty, I must admit that that quite a few of
my characters die an early death.  But when I get one to
the point at which the previous author recommends I start
polypiling, I'm usually set.  I admit I polypiled a bit last
game, but that's because I was stuck in the castle and needed to
make some boots of levitation (stupid potion ran out early
on me) which is one reason I'd rather not see polypiling
removed from the game.

Here's one solution: make rock moles and jello cubes more
frequent, so peoples precious polypiles get slurped up.

